=== entry d44da8acd919
kind: translation
rules: setup-pstack, model-role
intent: A budget moves each role's default effort by steps (large keeps it, unlimited raises it one, medium lowers it one, small lowers it two), clamped to the ladder, and each entry takes the highest effort its model offers at or below that target. Drops slug parsing, families, the `auto` alias, and the Claude, Fable, and Gemini slug examples. Keep "keep the user's changed roles on a re-run" and "mark a role needing a choice".
--- upstream
**(b) Apply it.** Build the working table from the skill defaults, and on a re-run keep any role you changed by family, list, or alias (`inherit-parent`, `auto`). Families are the ones Phase A of the **arena** skill defines, so Fable is its own family. Each role has a target effort, which is its default's effort moved by the budget. `large` keeps it, `unlimited` raises it one step, `medium` lowers it one step, and `small` lowers it two steps, on the ladder `max` > `xhigh` > `high` > `medium` > `low`. A target at either end of the ladder stays there. Most defaults are at `xhigh`, and each budget label names where those land. Set the effort token of every real slug in the role, panel entries included, to the role's target. The effort token is the last token, or the one before a trailing `fast`. If the result is not a detected slug, use the same family's detected slug with the highest effort at or below the target, else mark the role as needing a choice. `inherit-parent` and `auto` do not change. So `unlimited` turns `claude-opus-5-5-xhigh` into `claude-opus-5-5-max` and `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast` into `claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-fast`, and it keeps `claude-fable-5-2-max`. Gemini tops out at `high`, so under `unlimited` the fallback keeps `gemini-4-carbon-high` as it is. `small` turns the first two into `claude-opus-5-5-medium` and `claude-opus-5-5-low-fast`. Fable 5.2 and Gemini have no fast slug, so never write one.
--- patched
**(b) Apply it.** Build the working table from the defaults, and on a re-run keep any role you changed by model, list, or alias (`inherit-parent`). Each role has a target effort, which is its default's effort moved by the budget. `large` keeps it, `unlimited` raises it one step, `medium` lowers it one step, and `small` lowers it two steps, on the ladder `max` > `xhigh` > `high` > `medium` > `low`. A target at either end of the ladder stays there. Each budget label names where an `xhigh` default lands. Set the effort of every real entry in the role, panel entries included, to the role's target. Ignore effort options off that ladder. If the model doesn't offer that effort, use the highest effort it offers below it, else mark the role as needing a choice. `inherit-parent` does not change. So under `unlimited`, a model whose efforts stop at `xhigh` runs at `xhigh`, and under `small` an `xhigh` default runs at `medium`.

=== entry 25129b0b93db
kind: translation
rules: ask, setup-pstack, model-role, cursor-only
intent: Confirms roles in plain text with `inherit-parent` as the only alias; drops `auto` and Cursor's Auto. Keep the panel-list note, the cross-judge pool's one judge from another vendor in list order (Claude models are one vendor, an alias never judges), and the swarm note.
--- upstream
**(c) Show the roles and confirm.** Show every role with its model, marking any real slug not in the detected set as needing a choice. Also list each line step 2 dropped. Ask whether to accept as-is or change specific roles, offering the detected models plus `inherit-parent` and `auto` (both mean: this role runs on the parent chat model, which is how Auto users stay on Auto) as the options. Prefer AskQuestion over free text. For panel roles (arena runners, architect runners, interrogate reviewers) the value is a list, and one subagent runs per entry, alias entries included, so the list length sets the count. `arena cross-judge pool` is also a list, but Arena runs one judge. It tries only values from a vendor other than the parent's, in list order, so order it by preference. Fable and the other Claude models are one vendor. An `inherit-parent` or `auto` value never judges. `swarm workers` is the default model for every worker unless a race or comparison assigns another model per arm.
--- patched
**(c) Show the roles and confirm.** Show every role with its entries, marking any real entry not in the detected set as needing a choice. Also list each line step 2 dropped. Ask whether to accept as-is or change specific roles, offering the detected models plus `inherit-parent` (this role runs on the parent chat model) as the options. Ask in plain text, then end the turn. For panel roles (arena runners, architect runners, interrogate reviewers) the value is a list, and one subagent runs per entry, alias entries included, so the list length sets the count. `arena cross-judge pool` is also a list, but Arena runs one judge. It tries only entries from a vendor other than the parent's, in list order, so order it by preference. Claude models are one vendor. An `inherit-parent` entry never judges. `swarm workers` is the default model for every worker unless a race or comparison assigns another model per arm.

